From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:11:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: don't flag coding rate 2/3 in PHY
 control word 1

With B43_TXH_PHY1_CRATE_2_3 set, the HT-PHY transmits frames that no
receiver decodes, and reports no error. Among legacy rates this bit is
only used for 48 Mbit/s, so on BCM4331 every 48 Mbit/s frame was lost:
with the rate fixed to 48 Mbit/s nothing gets through, and rate control
keeps paying for retries at it.

Sweeping the coding rate field shows the HT-PHY takes the rate from the
PLCP header: any even value transmits correct frames, any odd value
fails. Clear the bit on HT-PHY only; brcmsmac sets it on N-PHY.

Signed-off-by: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
index f0b082596637..4de6e5042c55 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
@@ -186,6 +186,11 @@ static u16 b43_generate_tx_phy_ctl1(struct b43_wldev *dev, u8 bitrate)
 			control |= e->coding_rate;
 			control |= e->modulation;
 		}
+		/* The HT-PHY takes the coding rate from the PLCP header;
+		 * with this bit set it sends frames nobody can decode.
+		 */
+		if (phy->type == B43_PHYTYPE_HT)
+			control &= ~B43_TXH_PHY1_CRATE_2_3;
 		control |= B43_TXH_PHY1_MODE_SISO;
 	}
 
